From 00efeba1ffea0ae498c7a35e9133172b102cc983 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:21:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: rkisp2: Add the ISPP scaler stream

The ISPP path exposes one stream, the unscaled main output, so an
application that wants a preview next to the full-size frame has to
scale it itself. The ISPP has scaler outputs for exactly that.

Open the first scaler output and offer it as a second stream behind
the main one: any of the scaler's formats, no larger than the main
stream, 1280x720 NV12 by default. The scaler node is configured,
started and stopped with the main output, a request carrying a
scaler buffer queues it to the node, and the request completes once
both buffers of the frame are back.

A request is numbered as the frame after the one in flight, so the IPA
frame contexts and the statistics sequence stay aligned across request
gaps, and the sensor controls the IPA computes for a request are kept
for the next ISP frame start. The statistics path keeps reading the
values in effect for each ISP sequence.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
